# Kotlin + Conventions
- Prefer Kotlin idioms (`val` by default, small focused functions, data classes for models).
- Use Hilt DI: `@HiltAndroidApp`, `@AndroidEntryPoint`, `@HiltViewModel`, and constructor injection only.
- UI-related blocking calls are forbidden; avoid `runBlocking` in new code.
- Keep packages aligned to architecture:
  - `app/presentation` -> UI + ViewModels
  - `app/domain` -> pure domain models
  - `app/data` -> datasources + repositories + Result mappings
  - `base` -> shared UI components
- Follow naming from existing code:
  - RemoteDataSource classes wrap APIs
  - Repositories are the only place that orchestrates remote/local for a feature

